# No More Margin Hacks

Instead of adding margins to every grid item, you define the gutter size at the container level:
- `column-gap` – space between columns.
- `row-gap` (formerly `grid-row-gap`) – space between rows.
- `gap` – shorthand for `row-gap` and `column-gap` (if one value, both set to same).

```css
.container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: 20px; /* 20px between all rows and columns */
}
```
Gaps only appear between tracks, not at the edges of the container.

slides.codeSnippet:
.container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: 30px 15px; /* row-gap 30px, column-gap 15px */
}
